---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <p class="lede">
    This placeholder sets out the structure of Pynapli's Privacy Policy. Each section should be
    replaced with finalized legal wording before launch. Pynapli is strictly for adults 18 and over.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Account details, profile information you choose to add, approximate location used for discovery,
    device and usage data, media you upload, and messages you send. You control much of what you
    share.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
  <p>
    To operate discovery (grid, swipe, filters), enable messaging and matching, keep the community
    safe, prevent abuse, provide support, and improve the product.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Location</h2>
  <p>
    Discovery uses your approximate area, not your precise coordinates. Your exact location is never
    displayed to other members.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data. We share limited information with service providers who help
    us run the app, and where required by law or to protect safety.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your choices &amp; controls</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Edit or delete your profile and content.</li>
    <li>Control who can see and message you; block and hide members.</li>
    <li>Manage private albums — shared only when you choose.</li>
    <li>Request access to, or deletion of, your data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
  <p>Placeholder for retention periods and deletion practices.</p>

  <h2>7. Age</h2>
  <p>Pynapli is for adults only. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18.</p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? <a href="mailto:privacy@pynapli.com">privacy@pynapli.com</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
